<title>NEW ZEALAND: New Zealand ADRs firm as Dow ends flat.</title>
<headline>New Zealand ADRs firm as Dow ends flat.</headline>
<dateline>WELLINGTON 1996-10-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>New Zealand ADRs were firm as the Dow Industrials ended flat, down 1.12 at 5932.85.</p>
<p>Price movements of NZ stocks listed in the U.S., Britain and Australia.</p>
<p>Company	Exchange    Last	  Net change</p>
<p>FCL Bldg	 N.Y.    US$23 7/8	 +0 1/2</p>
<p>FCL Engy	 N.Y.    US$24 1/2	 +0 1/8</p>
<p>FCL Paper	N.Y.    US$20 1/8	 +0 1/8</p>
<p>FCL Forest     N.Y.    US$14 7/8	 nil</p>
<p>Telecom	  N.Y.    US$77 5/8	 +0 1/4</p>
<p>Tranz Rail     N.Y.    US$14 3/8	 -0 1/4</p>
<p>Guinness Peat  London  34		  -0 1/2</p>
<p>Brierley	 London  64		  untraded</p>
<p>NZ IT	    London  236		 nil</p>
<p>Foreign &amp; Col  London  158 1/4	   +0 1/4</p>
<p>Templeton	London  137 1/4	   +0 1/4</p>
<p>Lion	     Sydney  A$3.20	    +2</p>
<p>Goodman	  Sydney  A$1.34	    +2</p>
<p>Macraes	  Sydney  A$3.20	    nil</p>
<p>Notes - In New York, Telecom's American Depository Receipts are traded in bundles of 16 shares, while both the Fletcher Challenge shares are in bundles of 10 each. Tranz Rail ADSs are groups of three ordinary shares.</p>
<p>- London prices are mid-rates.</p>
<p>-- Wellington Newsroom 64 4 4734 746</p>
